{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically least largest clique by vertex index, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order; [] for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"empty graph. Self-loops and parallel edges are ignored. Each largest clique is searched for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from its first vertex v in degeneracy order, among v’s later neighbors, so memory stays O(n +"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"m + degeneracy²) however large a hub’s degree; of two cliques of one size, the lesser is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one holding the least vertex of their symmetric difference. For each v, a witness clique W"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(any one of the right size) guides a pass over the candidates in ascending number: a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"candidate in W is taken, any other is taken exactly when a search finds the rest of a clique"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"among the common neighbors left (which then becomes W). A v whose candidates all exceed the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"least vertex of the best clique so far is skipped. Exponential in the worst case."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximumclique()"]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Cliques\/MaximumClique.swift#L87","fileName":"MaximumClique.swift"},"symbolKind":"method","title":"maximumClique()","modules":[{"name":"Cliques","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maximumClique","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":